WEBVTT

00:00.620 --> 00:03.920
Rionne, do you know anything 
about the holy land?

00:03.920 --> 00:05.230
Well...

00:05.480 --> 00:09.110
Holy lands are cities that fell 
during the Dusk of Prosperity.

00:09.390 --> 00:11.660
This is my first time entering one,

00:11.660 --> 00:16.210
but I heard it takes several chosen ones 
to take down the monsters that appear within.

00:16.730 --> 00:18.340
Then we'll need weapons.

00:18.770 --> 00:22.080
Fortunately, I was teleported with this.

00:22.080 --> 00:23.500
The Skullface's sword!

00:23.880 --> 00:26.710
Good. That'll do nicely.

00:26.710 --> 00:29.730
I'm all set, but what about you?

00:29.730 --> 00:30.850
Do you have any weapons?

00:30.850 --> 00:33.120
Don't worry about me.

00:34.010 --> 00:37.570
<i>I can't let the princess find out
how strong I really am.</i>

00:37.570 --> 00:41.960
<i>If she learns I can use dozens of skills, 
she'll never let me leave.</i>

00:41.960 --> 00:43.020
<i>However...</i>

00:43.330 --> 00:48.120
<i>Getting out of here without using my 
full strength will be next to impossible.</i>

00:49.640 --> 00:53.520
The Holy Land, Calkia, has gates 
in the four cardinal directions.

00:53.520 --> 00:56.660
When our people inspected the city,
they entered through the south.

00:56.940 --> 01:00.440
There's a small door not far from it.

01:00.440 --> 01:03.790
Behind it should be a device
for opening and closing the gate.

01:04.150 --> 01:06.770
There's no need for us 
to wander through the city.

01:06.770 --> 01:09.790
I'd like to take a shortcut to the gate.

01:10.180 --> 01:12.330
What do you think of climbing the wall?

01:15.890 --> 01:16.550
What?

01:17.780 --> 01:19.680
What was that?

01:19.680 --> 01:21.720
Sorry. Let me try again.

01:21.720 --> 01:22.510
Sure.

01:24.730 --> 01:27.320
Rionne, how did that look to you just now?

01:27.320 --> 01:29.310
You definitely jumped,

01:29.630 --> 01:34.790
but you vanished once you were above 
the wall and reappeared on the ground.

01:34.790 --> 01:35.820
I see.

01:36.280 --> 01:38.320
<i>Am I being teleported?</i>

01:39.730 --> 01:40.670
Shin?

01:43.770 --> 01:45.360
What's going on?

01:45.360 --> 01:46.970
You're moving strangely.

01:48.520 --> 01:51.340
I know why now. Come with me.

01:55.340 --> 01:57.010
Found you.

01:57.010 --> 01:58.040
This is it.

02:00.820 --> 02:02.850
A ball of light?

02:03.120 --> 02:05.850
<i>It functions just like in the game.</i>

02:05.850 --> 02:10.520
If one of these is here, 
this entire city must be a dungeon.

02:10.520 --> 02:11.480
What?

02:12.020 --> 02:15.130
I've never heard of a city 
becoming a dungeon before.

02:15.130 --> 02:18.860
It <i>does</i> seem to work a bit differently 
from your standard dungeon.

02:19.350 --> 02:24.870
We can only reach the exit of this 
dungeon by following a set route.

02:24.870 --> 02:29.230
So you couldn't reach the rooftops 
or pass through the hole because...

02:29.230 --> 02:29.870
Yup.

02:30.620 --> 02:34.960
Straying from the route sends you
 back to where you were before.

02:35.280 --> 02:39.090
We'll have to follow those 
spheres in order to escape.

02:39.410 --> 02:42.110
I don't see any traps, so we just need

02:42.110 --> 02:45.430
to follow the spheres
and defeat any monsters,

02:45.430 --> 02:47.350
and we should be able to get out.

02:47.350 --> 02:48.650
I see.

02:48.650 --> 02:52.980
Forgive me for saying so, 
but I'm glad you got teleported with me.

02:53.290 --> 02:55.660
You saved me from having
to crack the mystery myself.

02:56.060 --> 02:58.860
The pleasure is all mine, Your Highness.

02:59.940 --> 03:01.360
Yeah, right.

03:01.720 --> 03:04.600
Now, let us find these spheres
and advance through the dungeon.

03:04.600 --> 03:07.930
Let me know if anything seems off.

03:07.930 --> 03:09.200
This is a holy land.

03:09.610 --> 03:11.780
There's no telling what could happen here.

03:12.200 --> 03:12.940
Got it.

03:13.380 --> 03:17.050
That sphere should teleport us 
to the next location.

03:17.050 --> 03:18.630
I'll go first.

03:19.150 --> 03:21.230
I'll come right back if it's all clear.

03:21.230 --> 03:22.700
Wait here.

03:29.970 --> 03:32.710
It takes you to a place not far from here.

03:32.710 --> 03:34.200
The vicinity is safe.

03:34.200 --> 03:35.240
Let's go.

03:35.240 --> 03:37.850
Sorry for saddling you with a dangerous role.

03:37.850 --> 03:38.900
It's fine.

03:39.310 --> 03:42.660
I couldn't allow a princess to teleport first.

03:42.660 --> 03:46.350
Besides, even if it drops me 
into a horde of monsters,

03:46.350 --> 03:48.670
escaping would be a piece of cake for me.

03:48.670 --> 03:50.150
<i>And even if they're dangerous,</i>

03:50.150 --> 03:52.770
<i>I can instantly slaughter them
if I'm not being watched.</i>

03:53.580 --> 03:55.400
I promise I'll repay the favor.

03:55.800 --> 03:57.570
Now, let's both get out of here alive together.

03:57.570 --> 04:00.370
Of course. Now, then...

04:05.570 --> 04:08.160
There's a monster around the corner.

04:08.160 --> 04:09.060
Got it.

04:14.560 --> 04:16.320
What is that?

04:16.320 --> 04:19.070
It's a ghost-type monster 
known as a Ghillie Waiz.

04:19.550 --> 04:22.040
It uses earth and wind magic.

04:19.690 --> 04:23.400
<b>Monster           Ghillie Waiz</b>

04:22.040 --> 04:25.210
It moves irregularly, so be careful.

04:31.970 --> 04:33.750
It opened with an unbelievable spell!

04:34.240 --> 04:36.250
So this is a monster of a holy land...

04:37.960 --> 04:39.500
I'll handle this.

04:40.020 --> 04:42.210
Rionne, try to land a blow on him.

04:43.330 --> 04:44.220
Understood.

04:44.650 --> 04:45.730
I'm counting on you.

04:53.530 --> 04:55.100
Good timing.

04:56.100 --> 04:57.770
You're mine!

04:57.770 --> 04:59.730
Flame Edge!

05:02.740 --> 05:03.990
Fiery Ashes!

05:08.200 --> 05:09.740
That should do it.

05:11.290 --> 05:13.310
That was surprisingly easy.

05:13.310 --> 05:17.110
The Skullface's sword is enchanted with light.

05:17.110 --> 05:18.750
That's the Ghillie Waiz's weakness.

05:18.750 --> 05:20.200
I see.

05:20.200 --> 05:23.380
By the way, Shin, what is that sword?

05:24.060 --> 05:25.730
It's called Kakura.

05:25.730 --> 05:28.330
It's a mid-tier mythic arm.

05:28.330 --> 05:29.390
Wow.

05:29.690 --> 05:32.360
You were hiding 
quite an impressive weapon.

05:32.360 --> 05:37.290
Well, yeah. Everyone should keep 
a card or two up their sleeve.

05:37.290 --> 05:39.400
<i>Of course, I've got more than one or two.</i>

05:39.400 --> 05:40.860
Huh.

05:41.460 --> 05:44.280
I'm suddenly very interested in you.

05:48.090 --> 05:51.410
How many monsters can you sense within range?

05:51.410 --> 05:53.290
More than twenty.

05:53.670 --> 05:57.970
Monsters typically don't leave 
their territory within a dungeon,

05:57.970 --> 05:59.630
but we can't let our guard down.

05:59.630 --> 06:02.640
It'd be great if we could reach
 the gate without issue.

06:02.640 --> 06:06.150
We should avoid as much danger 
as possible as we go.

06:06.150 --> 06:07.050
Right.

06:07.970 --> 06:11.570
<i>It's annoying that I can't
 flex my skills right now.</i>

06:12.040 --> 06:16.300
<i>Why do I have to play with restrictions 
when I'm not in the game world?</i>

06:20.490 --> 06:22.040
A ball of light?

06:22.960 --> 06:24.700
I'll check it out first.

06:27.330 --> 06:28.200
What is that?

06:28.740 --> 06:32.570
<b>Monster                     Gillslai</b>

06:28.960 --> 06:32.570
A Gillslai. We've run into 
a troublesome monster.

06:32.840 --> 06:34.070
What are you talking about?

06:34.070 --> 06:37.280
A large slime should pose
no problem whatsoever!

06:37.280 --> 06:39.040
Hey! Don't go charging in!

06:43.090 --> 06:45.380
What is this feeling?

06:54.500 --> 06:55.950
I told you so.

06:56.410 --> 06:57.570
Dust Explosion!

07:04.010 --> 07:06.440
I'm sorry. That was careless of me.

07:06.440 --> 07:08.110
I should know better in a holy land.

07:09.520 --> 07:15.760
Gillslai are nasty foes immune to 
bludgeoning, slashing, and weak attacks.

07:15.760 --> 07:19.120
They're also quite intelligent 
and will give chase.

07:19.610 --> 07:21.200
So let's defeat it here.

07:21.700 --> 07:22.880
Can you fight?

07:22.880 --> 07:25.880
Yeah. My life is in your hands.

07:30.720 --> 07:32.100
Flare Burst!

07:37.360 --> 07:38.220
Now!

07:43.690 --> 07:47.140
You destroyed its core 
with precision. Nice going.

07:47.660 --> 07:49.780
You did far better than I.

07:50.490 --> 07:55.610
Anyway, you're getting 
far more casual with me.

07:56.890 --> 07:58.350
It doesn't bother me.

07:58.350 --> 08:01.800
It'd be weirder if you were too polite, 
given the circumstances.

08:02.300 --> 08:04.490
Neither of us needs to hold back.

08:04.490 --> 08:07.250
Still, it's better to be proper.

08:07.670 --> 08:10.340
So this is just until we get out of here.

08:11.290 --> 08:12.260
Very well.

08:12.580 --> 08:15.640
By the way, Shin, 
why do you keep looking away?

08:15.640 --> 08:19.180
Well, uh... I can almost see a few things.

08:20.020 --> 08:21.420
What do you mean?

08:30.020 --> 08:32.110
Put that on.

08:32.730 --> 08:34.210
Did you see?

08:34.210 --> 08:34.930
Nope.

08:35.900 --> 08:37.180
Liar.

08:38.690 --> 08:40.120
Thank you.

08:40.120 --> 08:42.450
Are you always so thoroughly prepared?

08:42.450 --> 08:47.310
Where I'm from, we have a saying: 
"Forewarned is forearmed."

08:47.310 --> 08:48.960
Wise words.

08:48.960 --> 08:52.200
But I wasn't expecting you 
to have so many items.

08:52.900 --> 08:55.960
Well, you know. A friend gave them to me.

08:55.960 --> 08:57.470
Huh.

08:57.760 --> 09:00.480
So, I hate to ask when 
you've graciously lent this to me,

09:00.480 --> 09:03.730
but don't you have anything baggier?

09:05.030 --> 09:07.970
I mean, this is a little tight.

09:08.980 --> 09:10.650
It is?

09:10.650 --> 09:12.230
Oh, right...

09:12.580 --> 09:14.400
Hey! What are you looking at?

09:14.400 --> 09:15.900
Uh, nothing.

09:17.080 --> 09:20.250
Say, can you not use any magic skills?

09:20.250 --> 09:22.490
I can cast a few beginner-level spells.

09:22.490 --> 09:27.010
But surely they'd be useless 
against holy land monsters.

09:27.010 --> 09:29.980
I guess so. Hold on.

09:31.580 --> 09:33.230
<i>Schnee, do you have a minute?</i>

09:33.230 --> 09:34.510
<i>Yes. What is it?</i>

09:35.500 --> 09:38.000
<i>An imitation enchantment?</i>

09:38.000 --> 09:41.010
<i>Yeah. It's not as powerful 
since it doesn't use the regular method,</i>

09:41.430 --> 09:43.700
<i>but it'll work as a stopgap measure.</i>

09:43.700 --> 09:49.270
<i>I just wanted to make sure it'd be okay 
to teach the princess how to use it.</i>

09:49.610 --> 09:53.650
<i>Normally, I would stop you, 
but this is an emergency.</i>

09:53.650 --> 09:56.720
<i>You have no choice but to teach her 
as a method of self-defense.</i>

09:56.720 --> 09:57.780
<i>You're right.</i>

09:58.560 --> 09:59.530
Okay.

10:00.180 --> 10:02.080
I'm going to teach you some forgery.

10:02.080 --> 10:03.540
Forgery?

10:04.570 --> 10:06.680
Will that really be good enough?

10:06.680 --> 10:08.840
Yeah. You'll see.

10:08.840 --> 10:10.010
In that case...

10:10.010 --> 10:10.930
Fire!

10:18.410 --> 10:19.130
Here!

10:23.210 --> 10:24.560
It was burned?

10:24.560 --> 10:26.510
That's an imitation enchantment.

10:26.510 --> 10:28.960
In other words, a forgery 
of a real fire enchantment.

10:28.960 --> 10:34.180
It'll quickly destroy any weapon 
that's not at least legendary,

10:34.180 --> 10:37.850
but it's pretty useful even
if you can't use specialized skills.

10:37.850 --> 10:42.070
Are you sure you should be teaching me
something so valuable?

10:42.330 --> 10:46.320
If such a skill were more widespread,
fewer people would fall to monsters.

10:46.320 --> 10:48.080
I appreciate it, but still...

10:48.380 --> 10:52.940
You gave me this sword and refused a reward.

10:52.940 --> 10:56.340
I've done nothing but take. 
As royalty, it's humiliating.

10:56.340 --> 10:58.340
Don't scowl at me like that.

10:58.790 --> 11:00.960
You've acquired useful information.

11:00.960 --> 11:03.190
Shouldn't that make you happy?

11:03.190 --> 11:06.890
Nevertheless, I dislike taking without giving.

11:09.100 --> 11:12.480
Then in exchange, I have a request.

11:13.090 --> 11:17.730
As royalty, please protect 
your kingdom and your people.

11:17.730 --> 11:20.610
Everything you want to protect.

11:21.040 --> 11:22.060
Shin...

11:23.530 --> 11:25.480
That's all I ask.

11:27.120 --> 11:28.120
Very well.

11:28.720 --> 11:31.120
I hear you.

11:32.860 --> 11:34.800
<i>I managed to fool her,</i>

11:34.800 --> 11:38.590
<i>but imitation enchantments 
were actually an exploit in the game!</i>

11:38.590 --> 11:41.120
<i>But when she looks at me 
like that, what can I say?</i>

11:44.750 --> 11:46.270
We're almost there.

11:46.270 --> 11:47.170
Yeah.

11:52.650 --> 11:54.400
Hey, what's wrong?

11:54.880 --> 11:57.650
I suddenly felt like I was being sucked in.

11:58.000 --> 12:00.400
I can't say I felt anything.

12:00.400 --> 12:01.800
Really?

12:01.800 --> 12:04.200
<i>Something inside the holy land's
 drawing me in?</i>

12:04.900 --> 12:06.770
<i>What could it be?</i>

12:07.370 --> 12:08.630
Are you curious?

12:08.630 --> 12:12.310
No. We can't head back 
into the heart of the city.

12:12.310 --> 12:13.790
Let's keep going.

12:17.120 --> 12:19.610
Is that a monster egg?

12:19.610 --> 12:20.710
No.

12:20.710 --> 12:22.840
Normally, when monsters are born,

12:22.840 --> 12:25.390
the environment is warped 
by the concentration of mana,

12:25.390 --> 12:27.930
and the monster breaks out 
from the proverbial "shell."

12:28.940 --> 12:30.850
I've never seen anything like this.

12:31.310 --> 12:34.810
Which means it's no ordinary monster.

12:35.860 --> 12:37.890
<i>Between this and that feeling earlier,</i>

12:37.890 --> 12:41.560
<i>it's like something doesn't want us to leave.</i>

12:44.930 --> 12:47.200
Shin, it's emerging.

12:50.680 --> 12:51.800
A griffin?

12:58.750 --> 13:00.960
Is that... ice?

13:03.530 --> 13:04.340
Not good.

13:06.320 --> 13:07.090
Let's jump!

13:10.170 --> 13:12.450
It froze? Seriously?

13:17.230 --> 13:19.470
It instantly tried to mow
us down with its breath.

13:19.470 --> 13:21.240
Talk about ridiculous.

13:21.240 --> 13:23.000
U-Uh, Shin?

13:24.110 --> 13:26.650
Could you put me down now?

13:26.650 --> 13:29.490
Oh, sorry. It was an emergency.

13:29.810 --> 13:32.370
I swear, you're unbelievable.

13:33.080 --> 13:34.880
So, what should we do?

13:34.880 --> 13:37.000
Just getting close to it will be difficult.

13:37.380 --> 13:41.000
I'll act as a decoy.
You strike it from behind.

13:41.320 --> 13:42.720
Will you be all right?

13:42.720 --> 13:43.990
You can count on me.

13:43.990 --> 13:47.510
I doubt it'll hit me, 
and even if it does, I can take it.

13:47.900 --> 13:48.720
Got it.

13:56.020 --> 13:58.760
Hey, you frozen chicken! Over here!

13:58.760 --> 14:00.190
What are you aiming for?!

14:01.790 --> 14:05.780
<i>If I draw its attention, 
Rionne can try to catch it off guard.</i>

14:08.160 --> 14:09.480
Trick Throw!

14:10.960 --> 14:12.280
Where is he tossing those?

14:16.370 --> 14:17.290
Now's my chance!

14:19.290 --> 14:21.540
Tyrant Beat!

14:24.120 --> 14:24.980
All right!

14:30.430 --> 14:33.630
It only hit me with its wing, 
and yet it's still so powerful...

14:33.630 --> 14:35.090
Nice one, Rionne!

14:36.750 --> 14:39.440
If it's primarily ice, then how about this?

14:39.690 --> 14:41.360
Flare Burst!

14:46.650 --> 14:47.960
Did you get it?

14:47.960 --> 14:48.860
Yeah.

14:49.160 --> 14:54.130
The opening you made let me 
nail it with one powerful blow.

14:54.130 --> 14:55.370
Now we can leave the...

15:01.120 --> 15:04.690
Seriously? It can heal itself?

15:04.690 --> 15:07.370
I'm positive we defeated it.

15:07.370 --> 15:10.130
It didn't just heal itself. 
It completely regenerated.

15:10.130 --> 15:11.890
It's back to perfect health.

15:15.890 --> 15:18.030
How are we supposed to slay it?

15:18.030 --> 15:19.250
Well...

15:19.850 --> 15:22.400
Rionne, could you do me a favor?

15:26.010 --> 15:29.440
You want me to find the device 
to open the gate by myself?

15:29.440 --> 15:30.280
Yeah.

15:30.710 --> 15:34.270
I'll attack from the front 
and draw its attention again.

15:34.270 --> 15:37.390
In the meantime, you examine 
the opening mechanism.

15:37.390 --> 15:39.290
And look for what?

15:39.290 --> 15:42.040
Judging by its unusual regeneration,

15:42.040 --> 15:45.940
it's probably a monster made by magic.

15:45.940 --> 15:51.050
There's a spell somewhere 
regenerating the monster.

15:51.050 --> 15:55.190
And that spell has been applied 
to the opening mechanism?

15:55.190 --> 15:57.060
It's just a possibility.

15:57.690 --> 15:58.990
Very well.

15:58.990 --> 16:00.770
If I can open the gate,

16:00.770 --> 16:04.920
we could also temporarily 
immobilize the griffin and escape.

16:04.920 --> 16:06.990
It's an unknown monster.

16:06.990 --> 16:09.690
It might keep chasing us 
even if we leave the dungeon.

16:10.410 --> 16:12.210
But we'll roll with the punches!

16:12.700 --> 16:15.200
Still, will you be all right on your own?

16:15.200 --> 16:16.670
I can handle it.

16:16.670 --> 16:19.060
It's not my first time 
fighting something like this.

16:19.650 --> 16:20.990
I'm counting on you!

16:25.160 --> 16:30.720
<i>Sorry, Rionne. Honestly, it doesn't 
really matter if there's a spell or not.</i>

16:34.320 --> 16:36.260
No more restrictions.

16:36.950 --> 16:39.110
It's time to go all out.

16:40.350 --> 16:41.730
Limit Off.

16:54.970 --> 16:58.430
I don't know how much of 
my power I can safely unleash,

16:59.050 --> 17:00.910
but you'll make a good test subject.

17:01.450 --> 17:03.040
Let's see who can hold out longer!

17:10.010 --> 17:10.920
Found it!

17:15.930 --> 17:20.270
<i>I've defeated it thirty times, 
but it keeps coming back.</i>

17:20.270 --> 17:24.440
<i>Since it recovers from physical and magical 
damage, I'll have to try sealing it.</i>

17:27.100 --> 17:29.600
<i>What is that white sphere?</i>

17:33.170 --> 17:35.450
This is what I felt before...

17:36.690 --> 17:37.620
Take this!

17:41.710 --> 17:43.320
<i>It absorbed my attack?</i>

17:43.320 --> 17:46.460
<i>It's chancy to charge in 
without knowing what it is.</i>

17:48.210 --> 17:51.660
<i>But it's a chance I'll have to take.</i>

17:54.540 --> 17:57.460
<i>I'm being enveloped in golden light...</i>

17:58.240 --> 18:00.130
<i>The sucking feeling is gone.</i>

18:01.080 --> 18:02.240
I'll give it a shot.

18:09.820 --> 18:12.020
<i>It stopped regenerating?</i>

18:12.020 --> 18:13.570
<i>I don't get it, but you're mine!</i>

18:19.040 --> 18:20.070
Flame Strike!

18:28.580 --> 18:29.710
See you.

18:36.680 --> 18:38.810
Just what was that?

18:39.280 --> 18:40.460
Shin!

18:41.480 --> 18:44.530
What was that explosion? Where's the griffin?

18:44.530 --> 18:47.790
As you can see, 
I obliterated it without a trace.

18:48.460 --> 18:49.690
How'd you do?

18:53.660 --> 18:57.200
Thanks. Now we can say goodbye 
to this dungeon.

18:57.200 --> 18:59.140
Let's hurry out of here.

19:00.770 --> 19:03.620
We're supposed to meet my companions in Valmer.

19:03.620 --> 19:07.000
Valmer is east of the Melt Mountains.

19:07.610 --> 19:11.120
If we head toward the mountains, 
we shouldn't get lost.

19:14.620 --> 19:16.630
<i>So you safely escaped the holy land?</i>

19:17.010 --> 19:18.070
<i>I'm glad.</i>

19:18.650 --> 19:21.530
<i>And you'll be camping out tonight 
with the princess?</i>

19:21.530 --> 19:24.890
<i>Indeed, there's not much else you can do.</i>

19:25.210 --> 19:28.190
<i>What? I'm not mad.</i>

19:28.190 --> 19:29.050
<i>Goodbye.</i>

19:30.390 --> 19:33.320
Master, what's the matter?

19:33.320 --> 19:34.640
Let's get moving.

19:34.640 --> 19:36.400
What? Already?

19:36.740 --> 19:39.840
Shimmer, can you go even faster?

19:41.280 --> 19:42.550
Then let us be off.

19:43.900 --> 19:44.740
Huh?

19:49.640 --> 19:52.920
I'll keep watch first. Get some rest.

19:52.920 --> 19:54.040
Thanks.

19:54.700 --> 19:55.890
Want some tea?

19:56.340 --> 19:58.920
A tent, clothes, and food...

19:59.330 --> 20:02.460
Don't you think you're a bit <i>too</i> prepared?

20:02.460 --> 20:05.550
I was already all set to hit the road.

20:05.550 --> 20:09.680
And with an item box, 
it's easy to travel light.

20:09.680 --> 20:11.810
An item box, huh?

20:11.810 --> 20:14.520
I wish my kingdom had someone like you.

20:14.520 --> 20:16.310
Please ask someone else.

20:16.720 --> 20:18.820
You really won't do it?

20:18.820 --> 20:19.890
No.

20:19.890 --> 20:20.870
No matter what?

20:20.870 --> 20:21.950
No matter what.

20:21.950 --> 20:23.280
Can't you make an exception?

20:23.280 --> 20:25.570
No! Stop rubbing up against me!

20:28.760 --> 20:32.080
Am I attractive enough to fluster you?

20:32.080 --> 20:34.330
You mean you didn't do that on purpose?

20:35.050 --> 20:37.460
You really don't hold back, do you?

20:38.040 --> 20:39.840
But I prefer that.

20:40.140 --> 20:42.590
Doesn't that just mean I'm rude?

20:42.920 --> 20:46.850
As royalty, I'm used to everyone 
treating me with respect.

20:46.850 --> 20:48.570
So I like talking to people like you.

20:49.080 --> 20:51.850
Honestly, it suits me much better.

20:52.410 --> 20:54.100
What about your family?

20:54.100 --> 20:56.850
It's been a long time since we 
enjoyed each other's company.

20:57.490 --> 21:02.100
Maybe some part of me is 
looking for something to replace that.

21:04.160 --> 21:06.790
Well, I don't mind talking to you whenever.

21:06.790 --> 21:10.170
Hey, wait. Why are you snuggling up to me?

21:10.170 --> 21:12.210
Just while we're talking.

21:12.210 --> 21:13.500
Not bothered, are you?

21:13.500 --> 21:16.690
We couldn't let anyone at the castle see this.

21:16.690 --> 21:21.000
No. It's been a while since I haven't 
had eyes on me outside of battle.

21:21.930 --> 21:23.760
It's been a really long time...

21:24.070 --> 21:26.760
Sheesh. Just for now, okay?

21:28.760 --> 21:30.720
You're warm.

21:31.140 --> 21:32.270
Are you cold?

21:32.640 --> 21:34.600
That's not what I meant.

21:47.770 --> 21:48.570
Shin?

21:50.890 --> 21:51.850
Smoke?

21:52.200 --> 21:53.980
It's monsters.

21:53.980 --> 21:56.210
An absurd number of them have formed a horde.

21:56.620 --> 21:59.990
Not only that, 
but they're headed toward Valmer.

21:59.990 --> 22:00.960
What?!

23:34.970 --> 23:39.980
<b>Next Time
Episode 12
<b>Major Flood</b></b>
